+ADNI's placeholder identity affines establish neither anatomical
+orientation nor physical spacing. Its depth construction therefore uses
+unit source-array coordinates. The reference direction is the first
+array axis (axis 0, denoted $X$): projecting it orthogonally to the
+foreground's principal axis and normalizing gives the plane normal.
+The plane passes through the foreground centroid, with the same 0.1
+projection-norm rejection rule. In MedSAM3, labels are transposed from
+$(X,Y,Z)$ to $(Z,Y,X)$ for slice sampling; the coordinate mapping
+reverses that permutation before constructing the plane, preserving
+source $X$ as the reference. This convention assigns no anatomical
+left--right meaning to that axis.
